WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.813
Now let's translate business rules into relational

00:00:02.826 --> 00:00:07.247
decisions If every appointment belongs to exactly

00:00:07.274 --> 00:00:10.037
one patient appointment needs a non-null patient

00:00:10.063 --> 00:00:14.030
foreign key A patient may exist before

00:00:14.043 --> 00:00:16.279
any appointment is scheduled so the patient

00:00:16.306 --> 00:00:18.503
table does not require a child appointment

00:00:18.529 --> 00:00:22.681
row The same reasoning applies to provider

00:00:24.407 --> 00:00:26.209
An appointment may have zero or many

00:00:26.236 --> 00:00:28.854
service lines so those optional child rows

00:00:28.867 --> 00:00:32.835
belong in appointment service A service can

00:00:32.861 --> 00:00:35.269
appear in many appointments which confirms that

00:00:35.282 --> 00:00:38.190
appointment and service form a many-to-many
relationship

00:00:39.918 --> 00:00:41.220
The key habit is to read the

00:00:41.247 --> 00:00:43.536
business sentence first then decide where the

00:00:43.549 --> 00:00:45.878
foreign key belongs and whether that relationship

00:00:45.891 --> 00:00:47.299
is required or optional
